62
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:25,600
Well, in this week's podcast I have some email questions to answer,

63
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:29,520
And in answering one I'm going to spend a little bit more time than usual talking about

64
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:34,080
what I think is a pretty pivotal thing for us in scouting,

65
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,480
And that's going to take up the remainder of the podcast.

66
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:38,080
So let's get started. shall we

67
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,480
Send it by name

68
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,840
Email? that is, folks,

69
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:22,080
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

70
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:28,480
Frank Rodriguez is with Troop 436 in Long Valley, New Jersey,

71
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:32,000
And he wrote to say: some of the volunteers in my council seem to believe

72
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,320
that failure to have the Boy Scout handbook

73
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,719
with all the requirements initialed and approved

74
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:42,000
is a reason to deny an eagle at a border review.

75
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,640
I check the requirements and the guide to advancement

76
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:48,880
and I can't find anything that would support that position.

77
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,080
Am I wrong about this,

78
00:05:50,719 --> 00:05:52,240
Because it doesn't seem right to me.

79
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,520
Thanks for your help.

80
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,880
Well, Frank, it's really kind of simple, isn't it?

81
00:05:56,880 --> 00:06:01,360
If it was a requirement that a scout had their handbook

82
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:05,040
initialed and approved to present at an eagle border review,

83
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:09,840
it would be written in the requirements, right?

84
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,280
If you look at the eagle requirements.

85
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:16,000
it does refer to the project workbook in requirement five

86
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,240
and the application in requirement seven,

87
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,400
but there's zero about the handbook.

88
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,560
Why would the requirements be so specific

89
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,000
about a couple of other documents,

90
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,840
but it doesn't mention the handbook anywhere.

91
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:29,520
So requiring such a thing is adding to the requirements right,

92
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,040
And we're not allowed to do that.

93
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,400
There is a very simple statement

94
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,160
in the guide to advancement 2015..

95
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:37,040
It says: no council, committee, district, unit

96
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:38,960
or individual has the authority

97
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:42,000
to add to or subtract from the advancement requirements.

98
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,920
So that's an easy question to answer.

99
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,440
How does this kind of thing happen?

100
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:50,000
I mean, really, you know how does it keep happening?

101
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,440
I'm a little floored by this.

102
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,720
It's really kind of aggravating, isn't it?

103
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:58,080
How can, like reasonable people sit on an eagle border review

104
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:02,640
and think that they can deny a scout their eagle

105
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:05,039
based on the fact that he doesn't have his handbook

106
00:07:05,039 --> 00:07:06,719
and it's not all signed and initialed?

107
00:07:06,719 --> 00:07:08,560
I've run into things like this.

108
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,440
There's two basic solutions to things like this.

109
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:14,320
First of all, if it's not written in the requirement,

110
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:15,760
it's not a requirement.

111
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,680
Don't try and read between the lines.

112
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:20,320
Don't try and add things to the requirements. okay,

113
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:24,400
If it's not in there, it's not a requirement.

114
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,320
The second solution to this sort of thing

115
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:31,040
is going to be the solution to just about every problem

116
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,960
I ever hear about in scouting,

117
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:36,719
And that is simply being a champion of goodwill.

118
00:07:36,719 --> 00:07:39,200
Goodwill is incredibly powerful.

119
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,480
How do you get scouting right?

120
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,640
Well, you be a champion of goodwill.

121
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:46,400
You assume everybody's acting in goodwill.

122
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:51,680
Goodwill is a powerful antidote to a lot of things.

123
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,920
A lot of goodwill at an eagle border review

124
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,960
or any border review.

125
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,000
A lot of goodwill at a scoutmaster conference.

126
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,680
A lot of goodwill when we're sitting

127
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,440
and talking to our fellow scouters,

128
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,360
when we're working with our youth leaders,

129
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:05,280
when we're working with any of our scouts.

130
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:09,680
We have to assume goodwill on everybody's part,

131
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,760
And I talk about this on a regular basis.

132
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:12,240
but, come on,

133
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:17,120
I mean, this is what really makes life fun.

134
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:20,240
This is what makes being a scouter easy

135
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,480
and makes being a scouter positive

136
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:25,680
and wonderful and enriching for everybody involved,

137
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:26,880
including yourself.

138
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,960
You assume goodwill.

139
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:31,440
Now, your assumption of goodwill may be wrong

140
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,680
every so often,

141
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:36,400
but it's much less than you would imagine.

142
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,560
If you assume goodwill on everybody's part

143
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:41,360
and you work along beside them in that spirit,

144
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,000
you're going to get

145
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,440
you. every once in a while

146
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,800
you're going to get burned,

147
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,480
But isn't that so much better

148
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,200
than just burning everybody else

149
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,680
by assuming that they're trying to pull something off,

150
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:52,480
Right,

151
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:55,120
You know? here's something Baden Powell wrote.

152
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:55,680
He said:

153
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,280
Brothers we are to our scouts,

154
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,120
brothers to each other

155
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:01,200
we must be if we're going to do any good.

156
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:05,280
A luftness or jealousy could not exist

157
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:08,240
where there is the true ideal of brotherhood.

158
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:10,480
What we need, and what, thank God, we have

159
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,840
in most places in our movement,

160
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:14,640
is not merely the spirit of good nature,

161
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:15,280
tolerance,

162
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,840
but of watchful sympathy

163
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:20,080
and readiness to help one another.

164
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,680
We not only need this,

165
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,200
but we've got to have it

166
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,520
If we're going to teach our boys

167
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,520
by the only sound way,

168
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:29,520
and that is through our own example,

169
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,280
the greatest of principles,

170
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,160
which is goodwill and cooperation.

171
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,960
This next email- well,

172
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,840
this podcast- is being published around

173
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,080
the time of Halloween

174
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,480
and this is a scary,

175
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,000
scary scouting story.

176
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,000
It's okay,

177
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:48,560
It's all right,

178
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,280
It all comes out fine,

179
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:54,240
but it's a little scary in the beginning,

180
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:56,880
And I'm obviously not going to share

181
00:09:56,880 --> 00:10:00,480
any names or identifiers with this email.

182
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,480
But here's the scary, scary story.

183
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,160
I'm the advancement chair for my troop.

184
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:18,320
A scout gave me his blue card

185
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:21,280
And somehow I lost them

186
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:23,840
Before I could record the information.

187
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:27,360
the scout had earned several merit badges at camp.

188
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:30,640
The counselors do not retain their part of the card,

189
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:37,040
So I had all three sections of the blue card

190
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:39,600
in my possession and lost them.

191
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:49,920
You can imagine my dilemma: to record

192
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,600
or not to record these badges.

193
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,720
I don't have blue cards.

194
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:54,880
I remember that you've advised in the past

195
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,640
that we don't penalize a scout

196
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:57,680
for a scouter's mistake,

197
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,600
but I'm not sure it applies in this case.

198
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,600
I'm miserable about this whole thing.

199
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,360
What do I do now?

200
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,320
Oh my well, I had a little bit of fun with that

201
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,680
and I hope you don't mind.

202
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,920
Listen, it's not a big deal. okay,

203
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,280
Just record the merit badges,

204
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,640
make new blue cards.

205
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,480
note that they're replacements for the ones

206
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,960
that you lost on the troop copy,

207
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,720
Initial the scout section.

208
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,840
do what you usually do:

209
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,040
Give the scout their section

210
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:30,000
along with the badge. at the next court of honor,

211
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,920
And if anybody ever challenges

212
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:33,520
how this happened or what happened-

213
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:36,960
and listen, that is basically not going to happen-

214
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:39,600
Just tell them you had the originals

215
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,920
but you lost them before they were recorded,

216
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,760
so you recreated them.

217
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:47,200
You initialed them to show that you had seen

218
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,880
that these badges were complete

219
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,480
and they had the counselor's signature

220
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:54,720
and crisis averted.

221
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:57,280
Happy ending to a very scary story.

222
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,920
I mean, there's nothing magical

223
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,600
about that original blue card.

224
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:05,440
There's no reason that if a blue card gets lost,

225
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,720
that a scout has to go back

226
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,880
and start the merit badge all over again,

227
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,400
or something like that.

228
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,840
In this specific case, right,

229
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,760
the advancement chair had the blue card,

230
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:17,360
had looked at them,

231
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,480
saw that they were complete,

232
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,600
saw that they were signed,

233
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:21,600
but just ended up losing them.

234
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:23,360
And that happens from time to time.

235
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:24,640
You're not alone,

236
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:25,600
It happens.

237
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,840
And because they had seen

238
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:29,440
that these were completed merit badges

239
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,280
with a proper counselor's signature

240
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,400
and they came from summer camp,

241
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:34,320
so I wouldn't have any problem

242
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,920
of doing exactly what I described:

243
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,120
Just create one,

244
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,160
note it on the card,

245
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,840
lost the original

246
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:42,240
but saw the counselor's signature,

247
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,520
initial it yourself

248
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:45,040
and do exactly what I described.

249
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:47,920
Now, if a scout loses a blue card,

250
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,280
he's going to need to go back

251
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:50,160
to the counselor,

252
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:52,400
and if it's happening at summer camp

253
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,760
and they're not keeping records,

254
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,760
oh, now we're in a bit of a problem.

255
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,920
That's a really scary story

256
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,280
But, like I said,

257
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,320
I wouldn't have any problem

258
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,600
doing what I described.

259
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,120
And remember, this is just me,

260
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,440
but I think it's in the spirit of

261
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,480
what we're supposed to be doing

262
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:07,440
as scouters

263
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,880
And, as you said,

264
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,120
we don't ever make a scout

265
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,720
accountable for a mistake

266
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,240
that an adult makes.

267
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,760
And if you think that

268
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:16,880
there's any possibility

269
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,080
that there's a record

270
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,920
somewhere that the camp has kept,

271
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,200
well, you can follow up with that.

272
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,400
but let's not wait.

273
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,720
Get the scout the merit badge right away.

274
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,000
That's what's really important

275
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,960
And let's see.

276
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,440
The third and last email question

277
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,880
was a pretty simple one.

278
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:36,080
Do scouts still retire American flags?

279
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:37,600
Yes, that it still happens.

280
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,960
Some scout troops

281
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,600
have regular flag retirement ceremonies,

282
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,880
but this is something that

283
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:44,000
anybody can do, really,

284
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,640
because if you look at the US flag code,

285
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:48,880
it doesn't really specify much

286
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,040
about this, other than

287
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,280
when a flag is so tattered

288
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,880
that it is no longer fit to serve

289
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,800
as a symbol of the United States,

290
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:58,240
it should be destroyed

291
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:00,000
in a dignified manner,

292
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,360
preferably by burning.

293
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:03,520
So it doesn't have to be destroyed

294
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:06,320
in some big authorized ceremony of some kind,

295
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,600
because the flag code doesn't talk

296
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,200
about an authorized ceremony

297
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,720
and it doesn't talk about

298
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,120
particular people being authorized to do this.

299
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,400
The controlling thing there

300
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,960
is dignified manner

301
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:19,120
and preferably by burning.

302
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,360
So if we have a flag

303
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,640
that is no longer fit to display,

304
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,240
we don't just ball it up

305
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,440
and throw it in the trash.

306
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,360
We destroy it in a dignified manner

307
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,000
And, like I said,

308
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,840
check the flag code and tell me if I'm wrong.

309
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,440
but I don't see anything.

310
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:35,200
I'm sure you can find a local scout troop

311
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,720
who'd be willing to do that for you.

312
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,320
I know the veterans associations

313
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:39,840
are usually willing to take flags

314
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,920
and dispose of them in a dignified manner.

315
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:42,720
but there you go.

316
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,600
I hope that helps.

